From: kwatson@netcom.com (Kennita Watson)
Date: Sat, 2 Jul 1994 17:58:04 -0700
Subject: [#94-7-2] Zero-gee:  the best we can get -- for now

I just called a company called Interglobal Space Lines (how's that for
preempting a great name?) that offers a one-day certification program in
operating under weightless conditions, for both astronauts and civilians.

They take you up in an airplane that goes up and over into a ballistic
trajectory, leaving the occupants weightless for 25-30 seconds at a time.
This is done over and over (about 20 times as I recall from my phone
conversation), and they assure me it's nothing at all like The Edge.  The
whole thing costs (hold on to your hat, Hannah) $1950.

You can find out more for yourself by calling ISL at 307-739-1296, or you
can wait for me to summarize whatever else I find out from the literature
they're supposed to be sending me.

I've already been to Space Camp twice, and I just may start saving up for
this.  It ain't cheap thrills, but it sure sounds like it would be thrills.

Kennita



