Article 1120 of k12.ed.tag:
Newsgroups: k12.ed.tag
Subject: Re: What is 'Gifted'?
Date: 3 Jul 1994 04:55:36 GMT
Organization: Northwestern University, Evanston IL
Sender: awilson@merle.acns.nwu.edu (Andy Wilson)
Reply-To: awilson@nwu.edu (Andy Wilson)
Summary: Gifted is...

   What _is_ gifted?

Gifted is not easy.

Gifted is being ostracized.

Gifted is crying yourself to sleep every night and wishing for something,
anything, to happen to let you stay home from school the next day.

Gifted is being humiliated in front of your fourth grade reading class when
the teacher finds your "words I don't know from the book" list is empty.

Gifted is being told "Well, we just don't let freshmen take that class;
they can't handle it."

Gifted is taking the class anyway and getting the single highest grade.

Gifted is being told to be grateful that your teacher gives you extra
mimeographed sheets of busywork you've already mastered because "she's
trying to challenge you".

Gifted is being told not to raise your hand anymore after you get all the
questions right.

Gifted is being tucked behind the coat racks with a computer during math
class because the teacher doesn't have time for you.

Gifted is being yelled at for bringing home anything less than straight As.

Gifted is having the school that almost destroyed you try to take credit
for your achievements.

Gifted is being fought over like a prize when the class chooses teams for a
contest.

Gifted is trying to explain that wanting to learn is not elitist.

Gifted is being mainstreamed and being expected to "pull the rest of the
class along".

Gifted is struggling not to drown in a sea of resentment, pettiness, and
outright hostility.

Gifted is fighting to believe in yourself every single day of your life.




